\subsection{Multi-Threshold Classification Performance}

Table~\ref{tab:sensitivity_b1} reports Task~B1 classification metrics across six NVE thresholds. Task~B1 achieves $\text{AUROC} = 0.944$ because exp\_059 (NVE${=}4.72\times$, self-correcting CIVO, B1-negative) ranks above the sustained-CIVO positive 008d ($4.12\times$), breaking perfect rank separation. The optimal threshold lies in the interval $(1.62, 4.12]$; exp\_059 is the sole false positive at $\geq 1.7\times$ (accuracy $10/11 = 90.9\%$). Table~\ref{tab:sensitivity_b2} provides the corresponding analysis for Task~B2 ($\text{AUROC} = 1.000$, perfect separation with no false positives at $\geq 1.2\times$).

