\paragraph{Actor entropy dynamics under CIVO.}
Extended training of collapsed configurations reveals a distinctive temporal sequence: evaluation return collapses first, followed by actor entropy explosion ${\sim}35$K steps later. In the most severe case (EG~v4), entropy rises from $-5.21$ to $+3.22$ nats at a rate of $+2.11$ nats/10K steps, with returns declining from 583 to 93 between steps 60K--120K. A second collapsed run (EG~v5) shows $+0.61$ nats/10K with comparable return degradation (583$\to$102). By contrast, healthy baselines exhibit gradual entropy drift at $+0.07$ to $+0.22$ nats/10K---15--30$\times$ slower---with returns stable above 900. The return-before-entropy temporal ordering is consistent with the causal chain: delusional critic $\to$ bad actor gradients $\to$ policy destabilization. The entropy explosion is a lagging indicator; the NVE diagnostic detects CIVO onset ${\sim}35$K steps before entropy rises, consistent with its use as an early-warning signal (\S\ref{sec:appendix_sensitivity}).

\subsection{Selective Gradient Stopping and Gradient Decomposition}
\label{sec:sgs_gradient_analysis}

\subsubsection{Gradient Decomposition Results}
\label{sec:gradient_decomposition}

