\subsection{$\dt{=}1$ Imagination as CIVO Mitigation}
\label{sec:pathways}

Restricting imagination to $\dt{=}1$ while retaining the trained embedding (008e\_v3) eliminates CIVO in all four tested seeds (NVE $\leq 0.6\times$), confirming that multi-step imagination at $\dt > 1$ is the necessary trigger for the CIVO feedback loop. Three of four seeds achieve $64$--$94\%$ of baseline (eval $597$--$877$); the fourth (seed~0, eval $148$) exhibits CIVO-unrelated learning stagnation. This mitigation preserves the world model's ability to distinguish temporal scales (unlike embedding removal) while eliminating the imagination-side bias that drives value overestimation (Figure~\ref{fig:multiple_pathways}).
